for nearly 16 years youtube has been a  dominant force on the internet  billions of people log on to watch  videos from their favorite youtubers  some of which live right here in las  vegas eight news now reporter kate  houston spoke with two content creators  who over several years have become some  of the most popular youtubers  in town we have  a huge ambition a huge passion for  filmmaking and  acting for over 10 years hilly and  hannah hindi have parodied popular  movies and tv shows  such as stranger things in lord of the  rings on their channel  the hillywood show it looks huge and  well produced  and it's just us it's just us we're not  sponsored we don't have a network behind  us  and we do it all on our own the process  of producing a video takes months at a  time  with each parity uploaded anywhere from  six months to a year between each other  the channel has grown to nearly two  million subscribers with fans across the  globe  including the people they're parodying  due to high production costs the  hillywood show cannot rely solely on ad  revenue from youtube  so they're financially supported by fan  donations through the service patreon  which is a membership platform where  fans can get exclusive content through  their subscription  we are so thankful for the fan donations  we are so thankful for the fans  supporting us but  sometime in their life i would like them  not to  have to give i want them just to watch  and to enjoy  the hillywood show is one of many  youtube channels based in las vegas  like hillywood andrew foy has been  creating videos on youtube  for years i i'll always get these  comments and it'll be like i've been  watching since 100k i've been watching  since you were 10 years old  now 19 the fingerstyle guitarist has  amassed nearly 3 million subscribers by  putting out covers of popular songs  over the years foy has grown his channel  by adding vlogs q a's and collaborations  with his younger sister  that pushed the channel in a different  direction and it definitely  helped because those videos have done  really well foy says youtube is like a  full-time  job he's been able to use the money  generated from a partnership with  guitartricks.com  and ad revenue to help pay for college  his car  and build a savings moving forward foy  wants to continue to develop his music  here in las vegas my next big thing is  probably  creating original music a lot of people  a lot of people have been asking me for  original music as restrictions are  loosened the hillywood show hopes to get  back on set  and continue their conversations with  studios to take the show  even further even though we do  everything  we are at a point where we're ready for  some for a team kate houston 8 news now  now many of you may be wondering well  how do you create a youtube channel and  how can someone make  money from it well here it is the first  steps are fairly simple  on youtube.com go to create an account  and then just start uploading your  content  once a channel has a certain amount of  subscribers they can apply for the  youtube partner program this allows  channels to make money from ad revenue  from memberships merchandise  now while this allows content creators  to put some money in their pocket don't  forget  google does take a percentage of that  revenue  other channel will use the  subscription-based service  patreon as you mentioned there in kate's  story which allows fans to donate money  and support them  another big way to make money is through  a sponsored brand deal where a youtuber  will partner with a company  and advertise their product for more  details on the requirements for the  youtube partner program and to hear the  full interviews with the hillywood show  and andrew foy you can head to our  website at  8newsnow.com
 

